href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/sleep/healthline-scores-how-we-rate-mattresses\"\u003escored each mattress\u003c/a\u003e to narrow down our list even further.\u003c/p\u003e"},"mattresses-singular":{"metrics":[{"description":"mattresses evaluated","count":"250+"},{"description":"mattress brands evaluated","count":"80+"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate mattresses","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We fact-check health claims, evaluate materials, and look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline. The brand we feature in this article has passed our strict vetting process and has been thoroughly tested by our reviewers. \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/sleep/healthline-scores-how-we-rate-mattresses\"\u003eRead more about how we review mattresses.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"pillows":{"metrics":[{"description":"pillows evaluated","count":"210"},{"description":"pillow brands evaluated","count":"140+"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate pillows","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We fact-check health claims, evaluate materials, and look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo choose the products on this page, we considered all the pillows that passed our vetting process.\u003c/p\u003e"},"ed-telehealth":{"metrics":[{"description":"telehealth companies evaluated","count":"200+"},{"description":"online ED treatment providers evaluated","count":"20+"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate online ED services","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We evaluate services for consistency with standards of care and best practices, and we look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo choose the services on this page, we considered all the ED treatment services that passed our vetting process. Then, we \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/healthline-scores-how-we-evaluate-mens-telehealth-platforms\"\u003escored each service\u003c/a\u003e to narrow down our list even further.\u003c/p\u003e"},"ed-telehealth-singular":{"metrics":[{"description":"telehealth companies evaluated","count":"200+"},{"description":"online ED treatment providers evaluated","count":"20+"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate online ED services","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We evaluate services for consistency with standards of care and best practices, and we look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline. The brand we feature in this article has passed our strict vetting proces. \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/healthline-scores-how-we-evaluate-mens-telehealth-platforms\"\u003eRead more about how we review men's telehealth platforms. \u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"birth-control-telehealth":{"metrics":[{"description":"telehealth companies evaluated","count":"200+"},{"description":"online birth control providers evaluated","count":"14"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate online birth control services","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We evaluate services for consistency with standards of care and best practices, and we look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo choose the services on this page, we considered all the birth control services that passed our vetting process. Then, we \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/how-we-review-birth-control\"\u003escored each service\u003c/a\u003e to narrow down our list even further.\u003c/p\u003e"},"birth-control-telehealth-singular":{"metrics":[{"description":"telehealth companies evaluated","count":"200+"},{"description":"online birth control providers evaluated","count":"14"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate online birth control services","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We evaluate services for consistency with standards of care and best practices, and we look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline. The brand we feature in this article has passed our strict vetting process and has been thoroughly tested by our reviewers. \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/how-we-review-birth-control\"\u003eRead more about how we test online birth control services.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"},"fitness-apps":{"metrics":[{"description":"fitness apps evaluated","count":"55+"},{"description":"fitness apps selected as our favorites","count":"10"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate fitness app services","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eMedical Standards and Insights team\u003c/a\u003e has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We evaluate services for consistency with standards of care and best practices, and we look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo choose the services on this page, we considered all the birth control services that passed our vetting process. Then, we \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/how-we-review-birth-control\"\u003escored each service\u003c/a\u003e to narrow down our list even further.\u003c/p\u003e"},"hemp":{"metrics":[{"description":"hemp brands evaluated","count":"230+"},{"description":"hemp brands met our criteria","count":"57"},{"description":"hemp brands we've personally tested","count":"30+"}],"explanationTitle":"How we evaluate hemp products","explanationDescription":"\u003cp\u003eOur Medical Standards and Insights team has carefully researched and vetted over 11,000 products and services. We fact-check health claims, evaluate ingredients, and look into each brand’s reputation before sharing products and services on Healthline. The brand we feature in this article has passed our strict vetting process and has been thoroughly tested by our reviewers. \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/about/vet-brands-and-products\"\u003eRead more about how we vet brands and products.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}},"isPrependRecipeH2":false,"isRecipeRoundup":false,"recipes":[],"breadcrumbsV2":[],"hideTabs":false,"tabs":[{"id":"_noHeaderPrefixedContent","title":null,"header":null,"body":[{"tagName":"p","attributes":{"className":"h2"},"source":" Overview"},{"tagName":"div","attributes":{"data-preamp":"serena-chatbot"},"source":""},{"tagName":"p","source":"A sucking chest wound (SCW) happens when an injury causes a hole to open in your chest. SCWs are often caused by stabbing, gunshots, or other injuries that penetrate the chest."},{"tagName":"p","source":"Signs of an SCW include:"},{"tagName":"ul","source":"\u003cli\u003ean opening in the chest, about the size of a coin\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ehissing or sucking sounds when the person inhales and exhales\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eheavy bleeding from the wound\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ebright red or pinkish, foaming blood around the wound\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ecoughing up blood\u003c/li\u003e"},{"tagName":"p","source":"SCWs sometimes make no noise. Treat any wound caused by chest penetration as an SCW."}]},{"id":"first-aid","title":"First aid","isCollapsable":false,"listicleSection":false,"qaQuestion":false,"header":[" What should I do to provide immediate first aid?"],"body":[{"tagName":"p","source":"If an object is still protruding from the wound, don’t remove it. This can make the injury worse."},{"tagName":"p","source":"Call your local emergency services immediately. If no emergency services are available, get the injured person to a hospital as soon as possible. Follow any steps that the emergency services operator gives you. You may be directed to do the following:"},{"tagName":"ol","source":"\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSterilize your hands\u003c/strong\u003e with soap and water.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePut on gloves\u003c/strong\u003e or other hand protection.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRemove any loose clothing or objects covering the wound.\u003c/strong\u003e Don’t remove clothing that’s stuck to the wound.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eKeep a hand over the wound while preparing a dressing.\u003c/strong\u003e Protect your hand with a glove or other hand protection. If possible, have someone else put their hand over the wound. If no one else is available, have the injured person cover the wound with their hand if they’re still able to do so.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFind a chest seal or sterile, medical-grade plastic, or tape to seal the wound.\u003c/strong\u003e If you don’t have medical plastic, use a clean Ziploc bag or a credit card for the wound. Use your hands if you have no other option.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIf possible, ask the person to breathe out\u003c/strong\u003e to release any excess air.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlace tape, plastic, or a chest seal over any hole that’s sucking in air,\u003c/strong\u003e including entry and exit wounds. Make sure no air enters any wound.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSecure the tape or seal with occlusive dressing\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eor similar wrapping material that can create a water and airtight seal. Make sure the seal has at least one open side to let out air without letting air in.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRemove the seal if you notice symptoms of tension pneumothorax,\u003c/strong\u003e or a buildup of air in the chest\u003cstrong\u003e.\u003c/strong\u003e This happens when a lung leaks air into the chest and builds pressure. This can cause extremely low blood pressure (shock) and be fatal. Symptoms include crackling sounds when the person breathes in or out (subcutaneous emphysema), lip or finger blueness (cyanosis), enlarged neck veins (jugular vein distention), short, shallow breaths, and one side of the chest appearing larger than the other.\u003c/li\u003e"},{"tagName":"p","source":"Keep the person on their side unless this makes it harder for them to breathe. Let out as much excess air as possible from the chest while making sure that the person can still breath."},{"tagName":"p","source":"If the person loses consciousness or stops breathing, do the following:"},{"tagName":"ul","source":"\u003cli\u003eperform \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/first-aid/cpr\" class=\"content-link css-kxhged\"\u003ecardiopulmonary resuscitation\u003c/a\u003e (CPR)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003euse a blanket to keep them from getting too cold\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003edon’t let the person eat or drink\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eput pressure on wounds to slow bleeding\u003c/li\u003e"}]},{"id":"hospital-treatment","title":"Hospital treatment","isCollapsable":false,"listicleSection":false,"qaQuestion":false,"header":[" How is this type of wound treated in a hospital?"],"body":[{"tagName":"p","source":"Once the person has been admitted into the hospital, the following may be done:"},{"tagName":"ul","source":"\u003cli\u003eA facemask is placed over the nose and mouth of the patient to deliver oxygen into their body.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe patient is connected to an intravenous (IV) catheter and given anesthesia so that a doctor or surgeon can operate.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eDuring surgery, a small incision is made on the patient’s chest. The surgeon inserts a chest tube into the patient’s chest cavity (the pleural space) to drain fluids from the area around their lungs. The chest tube stays in until all excess air and fluid has been drained.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe surgeon then surgically closes the wound with stitches or sutures to prevent further bleeding and to keep air from getting into the pleural space.\u003c/li\u003e"}]},{"id":"complications","title":"Complications","isCollapsable":false,"listicleSection":false,"qaQuestion":false,"header":[" Are there any possible complications?"],"body":[{"tagName":"p","source":"Possible complications of an SCW that can be fatal include:"},{"tagName":"ul","source":"\u003cli\u003etension \u003ca href=\"https://www.healthline.com/health/collapsed-lung\" class=\"content-link css-kxhged\"\u003epneumothorax\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eloss of oxygen in the blood (hypoxia)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eshock from blood or oxygen loss (hypotension)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003efluid buildup in the chest cavity\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003einjuries to vital organs, such as the heart, lungs, or gastrointestinal system \u003c/li\u003e"}]},{"id":"recovery","title":"Recovery","isCollapsable":false,"listicleSection":false,"qaQuestion":false,"header":[" What is recovery like from an SCW?"],"body":[{"tagName":"p","source":"If an SCW isn’t treated quickly in a medical facility, it can be fatal."},{"tagName":"p","source":"Typical recovery from an SCW takes about 7 to 10 days, or longer if there are multiple wounds. Further surgeries may be needed to treat any punctures in the lungs, muscles, heart, or other organs that may have occurred."},{"tagName":"p","source":"Depending on how extensive the wound is and what other treatments are necessary, full recovery can take three to six months."}]},{"id":"outlook","title":"Outlook","isCollapsable":false,"listicleSection":false,"qaQuestion":false,"header":[" Outlook"],"body":[{"tagName":"p","source":"SCWs can be deadly or cause serious health problems if they’re not treated quickly. Doing quick first aid within the first few minutes, and getting the person to a hospital, can save their life and prevent long-term complications."}]}],"hasAffiliateLinks":false,"affiliates":[],"isDisclaimer":false,"isOwnedAndOperatedPresent":false,"propsFor":{"articleResources":[{"displayLink":"ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24048995","link":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/24048995","title":{"tagName":"span","source":"Butler FK, et al. (2013). Management of open pneumothoraxin tactical combat casualty care: TCCC guidelines change 13-02."}},{"displayLink":"journals.lww.com/nursing/Citation/1987/08000/OCCLUSIVE_DRESSING_FOR_SUCKING_CHEST_WOUND_.27.aspx","link":"http://journals.lww.com/nursing/Citation/1987/08000/OCCLUSIVE_DRESSING_FOR_SUCKING_CHEST_WOUND_.27.aspx","title":{"tagName":"span","source":"Carroll PF. (1987). Occlusive dressing forsucking chest wound?"}},{"displayLink":"ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK441885/","link":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK441885/","title":{"tagName":"span","source":"McKnight CL, et al. (2017). Pneumothorax."}},{"displayLink":"jems.com/articles/print/volume-38/issue-8/patient-care/treating-sucking-chest-wounds-and-other.html","link":"http://www.jems.com/articles/print/volume-38/issue-8/patient-care/treating-sucking-chest-wounds-and-other.html","title":{"tagName":"span","source":"Rathert N, et al. (2013). Treating sucking chestwounds and other traumatic chest injuries."}},{"displayLink":"webapp1.dlib.indiana.edu/virtual_disk_library/index.cgi/4931363/FID2617/DATA/operationalmed/procedures/treat%20a%20sucking%20chest%20wound.htm","link":"http://webapp1.dlib.indiana.edu/virtual_disk_library/index.cgi/4931363/FID2617/DATA/operationalmed/procedures/treat%20a%20sucking%20chest%20wound.htm","title":{"tagName":"span","source":"Treat a sucking chest wound. (n.d.)."}}],"byline":{"authors":[{"id":193,"name":{"display":"Tim Jewell","first":"Tim","last":"Jewell"},"link":"/authors/tim-jewell","type":{"value":"author","label":"Author"},"nid":"","specialties":[],"guestTitle":"","bio":{"text":"Tim Jewell is a freelance writer, linguist, and communications expert based in Southern California. At age 4, he read a book called “1001 Questions about the Human Body” and has since dedicated his life to breaking down the complexities and stigmas around the human body and the cultures surrounding it, especially in relation to mental health, sexual health, and gender identity. Follow him on \u003ca href=\"http://TimJewell16\"\u003eTwitter\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://www.instagram.com/diakritik/\"\u003eInstagram\u003c/a\u003e."},"avatar":{"title":"","width":200,"height":200,"src":"https://post.healthline.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Tim_Jewell_bw.png","alt":""}}],"medicalReviewers":[{"id":114,"name":{"display":"Adithya Cattamanchi, M.D.","first":"Adithya","last":"Cattamanchi, MD"},"userLogin":"acattamanchi","links":{"website":"","facebook":"","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/adithyacattamanchi/","twitter":"","instagram":"","tiktok":""},"link":"/reviewers/adithya-cattamanchi-md","type":{"value":"medical_reviewer","label":"Medical Advisor"},"nid":"122507","specialties":[],"guestTitle":"","bio":{"text":"Dr. Adithya Cattamanchi is an \u003ca href=\"https://www.abms.org/board-certification/\"\u003eABMS board certified\u003c/a\u003e pulmonologist who also specializes in critical care medicine. He currently practices at UCI Health and is a professor of medicine at University of California Irvine.\r\n\r\n\u003cstrong\u003eEducation\u003c/strong\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003eDuke University, BA\u003c/li\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003eUniversity of California, San Francisco School of Medicine, MD, MAS\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cstrong\u003eCertifications\u003c/strong\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003eAmerican Board of Internal Medicine - Pulmonary Medicine\u003c/li\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003eAmerican Board of Internal Medicine - Critical Care\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cstrong\u003eProfessional Accomplishments\u003c/strong\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003eResearched the epidemiology and management of tuberculosis in high burden countries\u003c/li\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003ePublished over 150 articles related to tuberculosis and other lung diseases in peer-reviewed medical journals\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cstrong\u003eAffiliations\u003c/strong\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.thoracic.org/\"\u003eAmerican Thoracic Society (ATS)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n \t\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://theunion.org/\"\u003eInternational Union Against Tuberculosis and Lung Disease\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e"},"avatar":{"title":"","width":500,"height":500,"src":"https://post.healthline.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Adithya-Cattamanchi-500x500-Bio.png","alt":""}}],"id":"wp-651099","updateReason":[],"factCheckedBy":"","factCheckers":[],"articleHistory":[],"articleDates":{"factChecked":{"date":null,"display":""},"medicallyReviewed":{"date":1512115200,"display":"December 1, 2017"},"published":{"date":1512115200,"display":"December 1, 2017"},"lastUpdates":{"date":1537245471,"display":"September 18, 2018"},"modified":{"date":1537270671,"display":"September 18, 2018"}},"type":"healthfeature","language":"en"},"readNext":{"items":[{"title":["What Is Atelectasis?"],"text":["Atelectasis is a fairly common condition that happens when tiny sacs in your lungs, called alveoli, don't inflate. We review its symptoms and causes."],"link":"/health/atelectasis","imageAlt":"What Is Atelectasis?","thumbnail":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Doctor_examination_lungs-732x549-thumbnail-732x549.jpg","isNutrition":false,"authors":[{"id":560,"name":{"display":"The Healthline Editorial Team","first":"The Healthline Editorial Team","last":""},"userLogin":"healthlineeditorialteam","links":{"website":"","facebook":"","linkedin":"","twitter":"","instagram":"","tiktok":""},"link":"/authors/the-healthline-editorial-team","type":{"value":"author","label":"Author"},"nid":"","specialties":[],"guestTitle":"The Healthline Editorial Team","bio":{"text":"\u003cp\u003eThe Healthline Editorial Team is a growing group of trained content professionals across the U.S. and the U.K. who are passionate about health and wellness and are committed to creating quality content and experiences by upholding the highest journalistic standards and providing comprehensive, unbiased, honest, and timely guidance.\u003c/p\u003e\n"},"avatar":{"title":"","src":"","alt":""}}],"reviewedByHeader":"Medically reviewed by","language":"en"},{"title":["Punctured Lung"],"text":["Learn about a punctured lung, including what to expect during recovery."],"link":"/health/punctured-lung","imageAlt":"Punctured Lung","thumbnail":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/874-Punctured_Lung-732x549-thumbnail-1-732x549.jpg","medicallyReviewedBy":{"reviewerName":"Adithya Cattamanchi, M.D.","reviewerImage":{"path":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Adithya-Cattamanchi-500x500-Bio.png","width":200,"height":200,"altText":""}},"isNutrition":false,"authors":[{"id":642,"name":{"display":"Becky Young","first":"Becky","last":"Young"},"userLogin":"byoung","links":{"website":"","facebook":"","linkedin":"","twitter":"","instagram":"","tiktok":""},"type":{"value":"","label":""},"specialties":[],"bio":{},"avatar":{"title":"","src":"","alt":""}}],"reviewedByHeader":"Medically reviewed by","language":"en"},{"title":["What You Should Know About Bibasilar Crackles"],"text":["Excess fluid in your lungs can cause bibasilar crackles. Learn more about the conditions that may cause this. "],"link":"/health/bibasilar-crackles","imageAlt":"What You Should Know About Bibasilar Crackles","thumbnail":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/766x415_What_Are_Bibasilar_Crackles-1-732x415.jpg","isNutrition":false,"authors":[{"id":639,"name":{"display":"Annette McDermott","first":"Annette","last":"McDermott"},"userLogin":"amcdermott","links":{"website":"","facebook":"","linkedin":"","twitter":"","instagram":"","tiktok":""},"type":{"value":"author","label":"Author"},"specialties":[],"bio":{},"avatar":{"title":"","src":"","alt":""}}],"reviewedByHeader":"Medically reviewed by","language":"en"},{"title":["COVID Vaccine Study Previously Blocked By CDC Is Out — Here's What It Found"],"text":["A COVID-19 vaccine study blocked by the CDC's acting director was published in a scientific journal. The study affirmed that COVID vaccines reduce the…"],"link":"/health-news/covid-vaccine-study-blocked-by-cdc-published","imageAlt":"COVID Vaccine Study Previously Blocked By CDC Is Out — Here's What It Found","thumbnail":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/covid_study_cdc-thumbnail-732x549-1.jpg","isNutrition":false,"authors":[],"reviewedByHeader":"Medically reviewed by","language":"en"},{"title":["A New Vaccine Was Designed by AI and Safely Tested on Humans"],"text":["A new vaccine designed by AI is the first to be tested on humans and may protect against a wide range of coronaviruses related to SARS and COVID-19."],"link":"/health-news/first-vaccine-designed-artificial-intelligence-tested-humans","imageAlt":"A New Vaccine Was Designed by AI and Safely Tested on Humans","thumbnail":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/vaccine_designed_AI-thumbnail-732x549-1.jpg","isNutrition":false,"authors":[{"id":587,"name":{"display":"Nancy Schimelpfening, MS","first":"Nancy","last":"Schimelpfening"},"userLogin":"nschimelpfening","links":{"website":"https://www.depressionsanctuary.org/","facebook":"https://www.facebook.com/depression411","linkedin":"","twitter":"https://x.com/about_depress","instagram":"","tiktok":""},"link":"/authors/nancy-schimelpfening","type":{"value":"author","label":"Author"},"nid":"","specialties":[],"guestTitle":"","bio":{"text":"\u003cspan data-sheets-value=\"{\u0026quot;1\u0026quot;:2,\u0026quot;2\u0026quot;:\u0026quot;Nancy Schimelpfening, MS, earned her master’s degree in community health education from Old Dominion University. She’s a freelance writer whose work has appeared in various online publications, including Verywell Health and Mindbodygreen. She’s also the president of Depression Sanctuary, a nonprofit organization that offers free support to people living with depression and other mental illnesses. You can follow Nancy and her work with Depression Sanctuary on Twitter and Facebook.\u0026quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{\u0026quot;2\u0026quot;:771,\u0026quot;3\u0026quot;:{\u0026quot;1\u0026quot;:0},\u0026quot;4\u0026quot;:[null,2,9684093],\u0026quot;11\u0026quot;:3,\u0026quot;12\u0026quot;:0}\"\u003eNancy Schimelpfening, MS, earned her master’s degree in community health education from Old Dominion University. She’s a freelance writer whose work has appeared in various online publications, including not only Healthline, but Verywell Health and Mindbodygreen. She’s also the president of Depression Sanctuary, a nonprofit organization that offers free support to people living with depression and other mental illnesses. You can follow Nancy and her work with Depression Sanctuary on \u003ca href=\"https://x.com/about_depress\"\u003eTwitter\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://www.facebook.com/depression411\"\u003eFacebook\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e"},"avatar":{"title":"","width":500,"height":500,"src":"https://post.healthline.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Nancy-Schimelpfening-500x500-Bio.png","alt":"Nancy Schimelpfening"}}],"reviewedByHeader":"Medically reviewed by","language":"en"},{"title":["FIFA World Cup: Biggest Health Risks for Fans and How to Avoid Them"],"text":["Experts say the 2026 FIFA World Cup could put pressure on public health guidelines for mass gatherings. Here's how to stay healthy if you're attending…"],"link":"/health-news/2026-fifa-world-cup-health-risks-protect-yourself","imageAlt":"FIFA World Cup: Biggest Health Risks for Fans and How to Avoid Them","thumbnail":"https://media.post.rvohealth.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/World_Cup_testing_public_health-thumbnail-732x549-1.jpg","isNutrition":false,"authors":[{"id":6392,"name":{"display":"Mandy French","first":"Mandy","last":"French"},"userLogin":"abaker","links":{"website":"","facebook":"","linkedin":"","twitter":"","instagram":"","tiktok":""},"link":"/authors/amanda-french","type":{"value":"author","label":"Author"},"nid":"","specialties":[],"guestTitle":"","bio":{"text":"\u003cp data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"\u003eMandy French has a master’s degree in both psychology and creative writing. She was a freelance writer in the United States for 10 years before moving to England. She is currently a Global News Editor with Healthline and Medical News Today. Follow her on \u003ca class=\"PrimaryLink BaseLink\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mandy-baker-0586/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eLinkedIn\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"},"avatar":{"title":"","width":500,"height":500,"src":"https://post.healthline.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/